.TH ZDOTS-MY-SYNC 1 "2026-07-21" "zdots" "zdots manual"
.SH NAME
zdots-my-sync \- zdots\-my\-sync doctor [OPTIONS]
.SH SYNOPSIS
See OPTIONS below (generated from \fBzdots-my-sync --help\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
Usage: zdots-my-sync [OPTIONS]
       zdots-my-sync doctor [OPTIONS]

Validate the ~/my directory structure by delegating to 'adots-my doctor'.
This command is read-only; zdots no longer creates ~/my directories directly.

Think of this as the Rails-style migration-status check for ~/my. Future
structure creation belongs in an explicit adots generator/prepare command.

Options:
  --my-root PATH          Validate PATH instead of $ZDOTS_MY_ROOT or $HOME/my
  --strict-public-vault   Treat a missing vaults/public directory as a failure
  --json                  Emit machine-readable JSON from adots-my
  -q, --quiet             Suppress passing checks
  -h, --help              Show this help
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
agent-guide(1), zdots-doctor(1)
